  "claim": "borg_init_flow_kill() (borg-flow-kill.c:3321-3335) skips uniques and tests non-uniques, whose max_num is never 0 (load.c:516-520, player-birth.c:421-427), so borg_race_death[] starts empty. borg_update() refills it on its first new-level pass (borg-update.c:2273-2287; borg.status.old_depth starts at 128, borg-init.c:519), but borg_think() runs borg_notice() first (borg-think.c:211) and sets borg.power after the update from that examination (borg-think.c:217), so BI_SAURON_DEAD (borg-trait.c:3131) is 0 in the reference and 1 in every candidate scored later in the pass (borg-power.c:1454 adds 2,500 per Mass Banishment scroll). borg_wear_stuff() (borg-item-wear.c:767, 995) and borg_drop_junk() (borg-junk.c:254, 449) compare candidates against that reference. Skipping non-uniques seeds the table at start-up, as the comment and borg_update()'s scan do.",
